# generated by bob
lib/

# React Native Codegen output is not committed. Gradle regenerates it into
# android/build/generated/source/codegen on every build, which is also the only
# way the spec lands in the com.ambirecrypto package that the Kotlin module
# expects — the script that generates shippable codegen hardcodes
# com.facebook.fbreact.specs instead.

# Cargo's build directory, ~1.6GB of intermediates. ubrn copies the artifacts
# that matter out of it into jniLibs and the xcframework.
rust/target/

# The compiled Rust. Built by the release workflow and shipped in the npm
# tarball, never committed — the unstripped archives are tens of megabytes each
# and a rebuild produces a fresh copy of every one of them.
AmbireCryptoFramework.xcframework/
android/src/main/jniLibs/

# Everything else ubrn produces — the bindings and the platform glue — is
# committed on purpose, so a clone can regenerate nothing and still be a valid
# package. Whoever changes rust/ re-runs `yarn ubrn:android` (and `yarn ubrn:ios`
# on a Mac) and commits the result; CI fails the PR if they drift apart.
